  "prefLabel": "Env-Wq 1019.01 Pressurized Distribution System",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wq 1019.01 Pressurized Distribution System.\n\n(a) An ISDS using pressurized distribution shall distribute effluent from a septic tank using small diameter pipe, with perforations, pressurized by pumps or siphons, such that the volume of water that flows out each hole is as equal as possible.\n\n(b) A pressurized distribution system shall lose 75% to 85% of the head in the network when the water passes through the holes.\n\nSource. (See Revision Notes #1 and #2 at chapter heading for Env-Wq 1000) #11184, eff 10-1-16; ss by #14486, eff 2-1-26, EXPIRES: 2-1-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wq1000.html"
